ram/send-failed` on the traffic stream. A synchronous\n+failure also answers `transport-error` to the caller. A failure reported\n+later has only the event channel (`dao.stream.md`, Writing). These events\n+carry no send correlation, so a caller must not count both the answer and\n+the event as separate failures. Each failed send occupies one traffic-ring\n+slot; repeated failures can evict inbound datagrams.\n+An address whose IP family differs from the bound socket's family is\n+refused before the host send as `transport-error` plus `send-failed`;\n+the socket remains usable.\n+\n+On Dart, a zero-length send is refused cleanly as `transport-error` before\n+the host is touched, with no `send-failed` event: a zero return cannot\n+distinguish an empty send from a failed one. S3 cross-host tests must not\n+originate empty datagrams from Dart.\n \n `close!` answers `ok`, closes the host socket, and is idempotent. The seam\n deposits `:dao.stream.datagram/closed` when it still can; the irreducible\n@@ -154,7 +166,7 @@ corner of `dao.stream.md` (Surfaces, observably gone) applies when it cannot.\n \n `:max-bytes` is composition data, default 1200, and is symmetric: an inbound\n datagram longer than it is dropped below the transform as protocol\n-validation, counted and never deposited. 1200 clears the IPv6 minimum path\n+validation, dropped, never deposited. 1200 clears the IPv6 minimum path\n MTU with headers to spare.\n \n ## 5. The traffic stream\n+   idempotent.\"\n+  [{:keys [identity deposit bind-host bind-port max-bytes]\n+    :or {bind-host \"0.0.0.0\" bind-port 0}}]\n+  (let [max-bytes (or max-bytes datagram/default-max-bytes)\n+        state (atom {:socket nil :bound false :failed false :closed false})\n+        announced-failure (atom false)\n+        mark-closed!\n+        (fn []\n+          (when-not (:closed @state)\n+            (swap! state assoc :closed true)\n+            (when (:bound @state)\n+              (deposit-event! deposit (datagram/closed-event identity)))))\n+        attach!\n+        (fn [socket]\n+          (swap! state assoc :socket socket)\n+          (.listen ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket\n+                   (fn [event]\n+                     (cond\n+                       (= event io/RawSocketEvent.read)\n+                       (receive! deposit identity max-bytes socket)\n+\n+                       (= event io/RawSocketEvent.closed)\n+                       (mark-closed!)))\n+                   .onError\n+                   (fn [e]\n+                     (deposit-event! deposit\n+                                     (datagram/send-failed-event identity\n+                                                                 (str e)))\n+                     (mark-closed!)\n+                     (.close ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket))))]\n+    (-> (io/RawDatagramSocket.bind bind-host bind-port)\n+        (.then\n+          (fn [socket]\n+            (if (:closed @state)\n+              (do (.close ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket)\n+                  (deposit-event! deposit\n+                                  (datagram/closed-event identity)))\n+              (do (attach! socket)\n+                  (swap! state assoc :bound true)\n+                  (deposit-event!\n+                    deposit\n+                    (datagram/bound-event\n+                      identity\n+                      (.-address ^io/InternetAddress\n+                       (.-address ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket))\n+                      (.-port ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket)))))))\n+        (.catchError\n+          (fn [e]\n+            (when (compare-and-set! announced-failure false true)\n+              (swap! state assoc :failed true)\n+              (deposit-event! deposit\n+                              (datagram/bind-failed-event\n+                                identity (str e)))))))\n+    {:send!\n+     (fn [host port bytes]\n+       (let [s @state\n+             socket (:socket s)]\n+         (cond\n+           (nil? socket)\n+           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+            :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"not bound\"}\n+\n+           ;; dart:io reports a send on a closed socket as a silent zero,\n+           ;; so the seam classifies from its own state: a real send\n+           ;; failure, deposited as the lifecycle event for observers\n+           (:closed s)\n+           (do (deposit-event!\n+                 deposit\n+                 (datagram/send-failed-event identity \"socket closed\"))\n+               {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+                :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"socket closed\"})\n+\n+           ;; A zero return cannot distinguish an empty send from a\n+           ;; failed one; refuse before touching the host.\n+           (zero? (.-length ^Uint8List bytes))\n+           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+            :dao.stream.datagram/reason\n+            \"dart:io cannot confirm an empty datagram\"}\n+\n+           (not= (str/includes? bind-host \":\") (str/includes? host \":\"))\n+           (do (deposit-event!\n+                 deposit\n+                 (datagram/send-failed-event identity \"IP family mismatch\"))\n+               {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+                :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"IP family mismatch\"})\n+\n+           :else\n+           (try\n+             (let [n (.send ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket bytes\n+                            (io/InternetAddress. host) port)]\n+               (if (pos? n)\n+                 {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n+                 (do (deposit-event!\n+                       deposit\n+                       (datagram/send-failed-event identity \"send wrote nothing\"))\n+                     {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+                      :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"send wrote nothing\"})))\n+             (catch Object e\n+               (deposit-event!\n+                 deposit (datagram/send-failed-event identity (str e)))\n+               {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+                :dao.stream.datagram/reason (str e)})))))\n+     :close!\n+     (fn []\n+       (let [s @state]\n+         (when-not (:closed s)\n+           (mark-closed!)\n+           (when-some [socket (:socket s)]\n+             (.close ^io/RawDatagramSocket socket))))\n+       nil)}))\n+               (catch :default _ nil)))\n+        family (if (str/includes? bind-host \":\") \"udp6\" \"udp4\")\n+        socket (.createSocket dgram family)]\n+    (.on socket \"listening\"\n+         (fn []\n+           (let [address (.address socket)]\n+             (when (and (not @failed?) (not @closed?))\n+               (reset! bound? true)\n+               (deposit-event!\n+                 (datagram/bound-event identity\n+                                       (.-address ^js address)\n+                                       (.-port ^js address)))))))\n+    (.on socket \"message\"\n+         (fn [msg rinfo]\n+           (when (<= (.-length ^js msg) max-bytes)\n+             (deposit-event!\n+               (datagram/datagram-event identity\n+                                        (.-address ^js rinfo)\n+                                        (.-port ^js rinfo)\n+                                        msg)))))\n+    (.on socket \"error\"\n+         (fn [err]\n+           (if-not @bound?\n+             ;; an error before listening is a failed bind: there is no\n+             ;; writer, and nothing else about this socket will be\n+             (when (compare-and-set! failed? false true)\n+               (deposit-event! (datagram/bind-failed-event\n+                                 identity (str (.-message ^js err)))))\n+             ;; after binding, an error event is a send or receive fault\n+             ;; this host reports only now\n+             (deposit-event! (datagram/send-failed-event\n+                               identity (str (.-message ^js err)))))))\n+    (.on socket \"close\"\n+         (fn []\n+           (when (and @bound? (not @failed?)\n+                      (compare-and-set! closed? false true))\n+             (deposit-event! (datagram/closed-event identity)))))\n+    (.bind socket #js {:address bind-host :port bind-port})\n+    {:send!\n+     (fn [host port bytes]\n+       (if (or @failed? (and (not @bound?) (not @closed?)))\n+         ;; A socket that never bound has no working send: Node would\n+         ;; silently bind a fresh port for it, which is not this socket.\n+         ;; A closed one still reaches the host, which refuses.\n+         {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+          :dao.stream.datagram/reason (if @failed?\n+                                        \"bind failed\"\n+                                        \"not bound\")}\n+         (if (not= (= family \"udp6\") (str/includes? host \":\"))\n+           (do (deposit-event!\n+                 (datagram/send-failed-event identity \"IP family mismatch\"))\n+               {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+                :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"IP family mismatch\"})\n+           (try\n+             (.send socket bytes port host)\n+             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n+             (catch :default e\n+               (when @bound?\n+                 (deposit-event! (datagram/send-failed-event identity (str e))))\n+               {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n+                :dao.stream.datagram/reason (str e)})))))\n+     :close!\n+     (fn []\n+       (try (.close socket) (catch :default _ nil))\n+       nil)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
